+- Only managers may freeze a project (`POST /projects/{pid}/freeze`); a non-manager gets 403.
+  Freezing sets every member's role to `viewer`, managers included, so nobody can
+  change the project's tasks afterwards. The response lists the members after the
+  change, ordered by user ID. There is no unfreeze endpoint, so after a freeze
+  nobody can freeze the project again (403). Other projects are not affected.
+- Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work). Freezing an
+  archived project is a write, so it also gets 409.
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
